OL,3,GNEWSABanner protest over 18 month wait
OL,4,Afor disabled bay
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man has installed a 16ft (5m) banner
OL,7,Fin front of his house in frustration
OL,8,Fover an 18 month wait for a decision on
OL,9,Fa disabled parking space for his wife
OL,10,Fwho is terminally ill with a brain
OL,11,Ftumour.
OL,13,FPaul Rapetti applied for a dedicated
OL,14,Fspace for Berta on Vine Street in
OL,15,FLincoln in March 2025 but, despite
OL,16,Fbeing told a decision would be made
OL,17,Fwithin weeks, nothing has been decided.
OL,19,FNow he has put up the banner, which
OL,20,Fsays there is a "disabled person in
OL,21,Fresidence" and asks motorists to leave
OL,22,Fa space free.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,387,380,200,160,0,100
